	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Undercity lies beneath the ruins of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}'s {link:capital-city}Capital City{/link}, in the east of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal Glades{/link}. It is the capital of the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} and the seat of their queen, {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link}. Its halls were carved from the sewers, crypts and catacombs of the old city. Green slime flows through its canals, bats circle its vaults, and its four great quarters ring a central court where the Forsaken trade, scheme and brew their poisons. No city in the world is stranger, and few are better defended.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The first tunnels were not dug by the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}. After Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} slew his father and sacked the capital, he meant to rule the north from its ruins, and he set the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} to deepen the crypts beneath the city. Then the Lich King called him to Northrend, and the work was left unfinished. When the Lich King's hold weakened, {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas{/link} broke free. With the dreadlord {link:varimathras}Varimathras{/link} bound to her service, she overthrew the demons who sought to rule the ruined kingdom, and she claimed the fallen capital for her people.

The Forsaken went below. They gathered the free-willed dead from the ruins above and brought them down to join their ranks. A stonemason named Bernd, rescued from the ruins, led the laborers who shaped the new halls. Goblin traders followed, and opened the first shops of the {link:trade-quarter}Trade Quarter{/link}. The dead of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} had a home again.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Undercity is complete, or nearly so, and it is full. From the {link:royal-quarter}Royal Quarter{/link}, {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas{/link} wages war against the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} and against the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link}. {link:varimathras}Varimathras{/link} commands the city's defense. In the {link:the-apothecarium}Apothecarium{/link}, the {link:royal-apothecary-society}Royal Apothecary Society{/link} labors on a new plague that the Dark Lady has ordered. The city has joined the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and receives its orcs, trolls and {link:tauren}tauren{/link}, who find it unsettling. Its people also remember a recent terror. Not long ago the necropolis {red:naxxramas}Naxxramas{/red} came against the city, and the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} fought it on the surface of the ruins. Many fell there, among them the captain of the Deathguard.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} Citizens, soldiers and scholars of the dead kingdom, many of them the folk of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}'s own capital.
• {b}The {link:royal-apothecary-society}Royal Apothecary Society{/link}.{/b} The chemists of the {link:the-apothecarium}Apothecarium{/link}, with their prisoners and their abominations.
• {b}The Deathguard and the Royal Dreadguard.{/b} The soldiers of the city and the guards of the throne.
• {b}Goblins.{/b} Traders and barbers who came when the city was young and have done very well since.
• {b}The dark rangers.{/b} Undead elves who serve {link:sylvanas-windrunner}the Dark Lady{/link} and remember {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:capital-city}Capital City{/link}.{/b} For centuries the kings of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} ruled from the palace above.
• {b}The Fall.{/b} In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} murdered King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} and gave the city to the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. That was the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}.
• {b}The Tunnels.{/b} The Scourge began to carve catacombs beneath the city, and left them unfinished.
• {b}The Founding.{/b} {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas{/link} and her {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} claimed the ruins and built their city below.
• {b}The Scarlet Assault.{/b} About a year after the founding, the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} broke into the Undercity through its walls, and the Deathguard drove them out.
• {b}The Necropolis.{/b} When Naxxramas struck, the Forsaken and the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} fought it together above the city.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the City",
			text = [=[• The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} say that the goblin {link:glix-xizzix}Glix Xizzix{/link} fed the city's hungry and armed its defenders in the war against the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. Glix is the one who says it most often.
• Near {link:sylvanas-windrunner}the Dark Lady{/link}'s throne, a lament of the high elves can sometimes be heard. It is a song of the fallen homeland she once defended.]=],
		},
	},
})

